F-1 Student Visa, OPT & STEM OPT
Millions of international students graduate from US universities every year. Their work auth follows a specific path. Know each stage — this is one of the most common work auth types you will encounter in IT and tech recruiting.
Stage 1
F-1 Active (In School)
Full-time student status. On-campus work only (≤20 hrs/week during semester). Cannot work off-campus without OPT or CPT. CPT: 12-month integrated work during curriculum.
→
Stage 2
OPT (12 months)
Post-graduation work auth. Valid for ANY employer — not tied to one company. Must use within 14 months of graduation. Does NOT require employer sponsorship.
→
Stage 3
STEM OPT (+24 months)
STEM field graduates only (CS, Engineering, Math, Science). Additional 24 months = 36 months total. Employer must be E-Verify enrolled. Must have Form I-983 training plan.
→
Stage 4
H-1B (if sponsored)
Employer files H-1B petition. Annual lottery cap: 85,000 visas. If approved: 3+3 years. If denied or no sponsor: must depart US.
Your OPT/STEM OPT Recruiter Checklist
•	Ask: "What type of work auth do you have?" → if OPT, ask: "Is it standard OPT or STEM OPT?"
•	Ask: "What is your EAD expiry date?" — this is the hard deadline for the placement
•	Check: Will the contract end BEFORE the EAD expires? If contract = 6 months and OPT expires in 4 months → DO NOT SUBMIT without flagging
•	Ask: "Have you applied for H-1B sponsorship?" → if yes, what is the status? Pending lottery may create a gap.
•	Understand Cap-Gap: OPT expires April 1 + H-1B filed + receipt notice = automatic extension until October 1 (H-1B start date). Candidate can continue working during cap-gap ONLY with I-20 extension and valid I-797C receipt notice.
OPT/STEM OPT Placement Risks
Risk 1
EAD Expires Mid-Contract
If OPT expires before contract ends, the candidate must stop working. The MSP will immediately remove them. Always verify expiry covers the full contract period — and add a buffer month.
Risk 2
No STEM Extension
Not all STEM fields qualify. The employer must be E-Verify enrolled for STEM OPT. If the employer isn't enrolled, the STEM extension is invalid. Verify E-Verify status before placing.
Risk 3
H-1B Lottery Denial
If the candidate is in the lottery and doesn't win, they must depart after OPT expires. You may lose a placed candidate mid-contract. Flag any OPT candidate with an active lottery petition to your manager.
