Green Card & EAD — The Best Work Auth Outcomes
Green Card holders have unlimited work authorisation. EAD holders have temporary but flexible work authorisation. Know the difference intimately — these two categories dominate your daily submissions.
Green Card
Permanent Resident Card — Form I-551
GC
StatusLawful Permanent Resident (LPR). Not a visa — a permanent immigration status.
Work AuthUnlimited. Any employer, any role, any time. No sponsorship, no expiry, no restrictions.
Physical CardCredit-card size. Predominantly green with Statue of Liberty holographic image. Expires every 10 years (for renewal — status itself is permanent).
I-9 VerificationList A document — satisfies both identity AND work authorisation. No additional documents needed.
PathwaysEmployment-based (EB-1 to EB-5) · Family-sponsored · Refugee/Asylee · Diversity Visa Lottery
🌟 Green Card = the recruiter's dream. Prioritise GC candidates for submission. No expiry tracking, no employer dependency, no transfer delays. When you find a Green Card candidate who matches the req, submit first — every other agency is also looking for them.
EAD
Employment Authorization Document — Form I-766
EAD
StatusTemporary work permit issued to various immigration categories — OPT graduates, H-4 dependents, pending GC applicants, asylees, DACA recipients.
Work AuthDepends on category. Most EADs allow any employer. H-4 EAD is restricted. Always check the visa category printed on the card.
Physical CardCredit-card size. Predominantly red (2017+ design) with bald eagle holographic image. Expiry date is CRITICAL — employment stops when EAD expires.
Key QuestionAlways ask: "What is your EAD expiry date?" and "What category is your EAD?" The category tells you the underlying immigration status.
⚠️ GC-EAD is a special case: some candidates have an EAD based on a pending green card application (Form I-485). These candidates may also hold an active H-1B simultaneously — they use the EAD for employer flexibility and keep H-1B as backup. Strong work auth position from a recruiter's perspective.
GC vs EAD — Quick Comparison
Attribute	Green Card (I-551)	EAD (I-766)
Work Auth	Unlimited, any employer	Depends on category — usually any, but confirm
Expiry	10 yrs (for renewal — status permanent)	1–2 years — employment STOPS at expiry
Employer Change	Freely — no notification required	Usually free — some categories restricted
International Travel	Yes — with valid GC	Varies — some need Advance Parole
Path to Citizenship	Yes — after 3–5 years	Depends on underlying status
