TN, L-1 & O-1 — Other Visa Types
Less common than H-1B or Green Card — but you will see these on resumes. Know what each means and how to handle them on a call.
TN Visa
NAFTA/USMCA Professional
TN
WhoCanadian and Mexican citizens ONLY — under USMCA (formerly NAFTA)
OccupationsSpecific professional roles: engineers, accountants, scientists, computer systems analysts, lawyers, nurses, pharmacists
Duration3 years, renewable indefinitely in 3-year increments — no maximum
AdvantageNo lottery, no annual cap. Canadian citizens can self-petition at the border. Very fast processing.
Employer-TiedYes — tied to specific employer and job title. Changing employers requires a new TN.
TN is the most underrated option in US staffing. Canadian citizens can get a TN at the border in ONE DAY — no petition, no lottery, no waiting. For urgent reqs where H-1B transfers take too long, a TN-eligible Canadian can start almost immediately.
L-1 Visa
Intracompany Transfer
L1
WhoManagers/executives (L-1A) or specialised knowledge workers (L-1B) transferred within the same multinational company
RequirementEmployee must have worked for the company 1+ year in the past 3 years at a foreign office
DurationL-1A: up to 7 years. L-1B: up to 5 years
GC PathL-1A holders can pursue EB-1C (multinational manager) green card — faster track than EB-2/EB-3
Tied ToSpecific company ONLY — cannot change employers on L-1
L-1 candidates typically work for large multinationals — IBM, Infosys, Tata, Wipro, Cognizant. If they say L-1 and are looking at your contract, ask who their current L-1 sponsor is. The L-1 needs to be transferred or they need to move to a different visa.
O-1 Visa
Extraordinary Ability
O1
WhoIndividuals with extraordinary ability in sciences, arts, business, athletics, or media — demonstrated through awards, publications, peer recognition
Duration3 years initial + 1-year extensions (no maximum)
AdvantageNo annual cap, no lottery. Can self-petition in some cases.
Work AuthTied to specific employer/agent who files the petition
O-1 holders are typically senior and specialised (researchers, executives, specialists). If you see this on a resume, it signals a high-value candidate. Work auth situation is similar to H-1B — employer-tied, transfer needed. Flag to manager.
